Typhoon H480 model provenance

The fuselage, propellers and original CGO3 geometry were adapted from
PX4-SITL_gazebo-classic at ab7dbc572b4519238f8263ef4a288e6eb80a6076.
The author named in model.config is Lorenz Meier. The original import
and the CGO3 addition are both attributed to him in the upstream history.
The PteroSim adaptation converts the STL files to GLB and adds new
materials, rebuilt skids, lens details and a newly modelled battery case.
The gimbal is x500's CGO3: the gimbal model of PX4's gz collection
(Tools/simulation/gz/models/gimbal, by Stefano Colli, Auterion), converted,
welded, shaded smooth and textured as x500's NOTICE describes. That model is
distributed under the BSD 3-Clause License; LICENSE.gimbal holds its text and
copyright notice.

The body is rebuilt from the source's main_body_remeshed_v3.stl, whose
surface is open along networks of cracks: it is the surface standing 0.7 mm
off that mesh (an unsigned distance field on a 0.5 mm grid), closed and free
of cracks, decimated to 300,000 triangles. The six motor pods, whose source
surface had holes the size of a finger tip, are turned anew from the source's
own profile about each motor axis. Normals are smoothed across edges under
30 degrees. The shell texture drops the bars beside the word, which hid half
of the T and the N's right stem.
The body's two materials are split along clean lines through the mesh,
and each propeller hand sits on the rotors that turn its way; the source
model mounts its clockwise blades on the counter-clockwise rotors.

